From b20db8f346f4c2f86b26d5bafcbbe36c112b3aee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:52:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0191 -- GetDeviceBuf abandons the iteration when
 the SB ring has no room for a chunk

WHY: DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice copies a chunk into the ISR ring with no room check of its own, and
two writers reach it. SDL_DOSAudioPump() (patch 0067) calls SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate()
directly with no WaitDevice at all, and looks at room only afterwards, for its return value. The
background thread's while (Iterate()) WaitDevice() loop does check room, but in WaitDevice, which
runs WITHOUT device->lock and, on the room-available path, calls DOS_Yield() (patch 0086) before
returning -- so the main thread can pump into that last free chunk, and the thread's Iterate then
writes into a full ring. Either way the write lands on the chunk the IRQ handler plays next.
Measured with patch 0190's counter (dosags, PLAN.md step 8, 2026-09-22): 5 Days in play under
DOSBox-X with the SB16 emulated, overwrites=38 and 19, peak fill 1625 and 1578 ms against a 743 ms
ring; AGS Quest, whose music is SB PCM, 1237-3350 overwrites per run and peak fill 50-148 s. A
first version of this patch put the check at the top of SDL_DOSAudioPump; it cut those to 0 on
5 Days but left overwrites=1, peak 789/743 (capacity plus one chunk), in every AGS Quest run --
the WaitDevice-yield path above. The check has to sit where both writers pass under the lock.

WHAT: at the top of DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf -- called by SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate with
device->lock held, before the stream pull and before PlayDevice -- if
ring_size - (ring_write - isr_ring_read) < chunk_size, set *buffer_size = 0 and return. SDL's core
treats buffer_size == 0 as "abandon this iteration, try again next time" (SDL_audio.c, the WASAPI
convention): no stream pull, no PlayDevice. The mixed data stays in the bound stream until the ISR
frees a chunk. The pump-side check of the first version is dropped: with the gate here it only
saved one recursive lock and a function call.

This is NOT the SDL/0050 gate that 0054 (Shape A) removed from this same function (see the comment
above the new block). 0050 returned buffer_size = 0 when no bound stream had data, which is exactly
the moment a pull is needed to make SDL3_mixer's MixerCallback produce SFX, so SFX went silent for
the whole session under OPL3. This gate never looks at the streams. It holds only while the ring is
full -- at least ring_size - chunk_size of audio is already queued for the ISR -- and releases as
soon as the ISR drains one chunk (~46 ms at 11025 Hz). With room, behaviour is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index ec3392b36..7096279c5 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -3760,7 +3760,30 @@ static Uint8 *DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf(SDL_AudioDevice *device, int *buffer_
        in tree for documentation per `pressure_test_tidy_narratives.md`
        -- fixing-the-wrong-layer is a useful negative-result reference),
        SDL/0053 (BeginShutdown semantic preserved). */
-    (void)buffer_size; /* unchanged; ring writes happen in PlayDevice */
+    (void)buffer_size; /* unchanged unless the ring is full (0191, below) */
+
+    /* DOS-PORT patch 0191: no room in the ISR ring for one chunk -> abandon
+       this iteration before the mix pull (SDL_audio.c: buffer_size == 0 means
+       "try again next time"; the core skips the stream pull AND PlayDevice).
+       PlayDevice has no room check of its own, and this is the one point
+       both writers pass under device->lock: the background thread's Iterate
+       (whose WaitDevice room check runs unlocked and then yields) and
+       SDL_DOSAudioPump's Iterate (which has no WaitDevice at all). The mixed
+       data stays in the bound stream until the ISR frees a chunk.
+       NOT the SDL/0050 gate that Shape A removed (comment above): that one
+       gated on "no bound stream has data", which is exactly when a pull is
+       needed to make the mixer callback produce SFX, so SFX went silent.
+       This gates only on "the ring is full" -- there is always at least
+       ring_size - chunk_size of audio queued for the ISR -- and it releases
+       as soon as the ISR drains one chunk (~46 ms at 11025 Hz). The stream
+       being empty never holds it. */
+    {
+        struct SDL_PrivateAudioData *hidden = device->hidden;
+        if ((hidden->ring_size - (hidden->ring_write - isr_ring_read)) < hidden->chunk_size) {
+            *buffer_size = 0;
+            return hidden->staging_buffer;
+        }
+    }
 
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0064, SFX-stall instrumentation
        part C): open the per-invocation SDL-DOS audio-callback timing
